From 8e1ade707a4ee6d11eaf04420852032b248f14fa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Xilin Wu <sophon@radxa.com>
Date: Mon, 27 Apr 2026 09:50:03 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 081/268] docs: Describe platform_profile as a generic class

The platform profile core now exposes the per-handler class interface
independently of ACPI.  Document /sys/class/platform-profile as the
generic interface and describe /sys/firmware/acpi/platform_profile as the
legacy aggregate interface that is available only when the ACPI firmware
sysfs hierarchy exists.

Signed-off-by: Xilin Wu <sophon@radxa.com>
---
 .../ABI/testing/sysfs-class-platform-profile  |  4 +--
 .../ABI/testing/sysfs-platform_profile        | 15 ++++++---
 .../userspace-api/sysfs-platform_profile.rst  | 32 ++++++++++---------
 3 files changed, 30 insertions(+), 21 deletions(-)

--- a/Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-class-platform-profile
+++ b/Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-class-platform-profile
@@ -32,8 +32,8 @@ What:		/sys/class/platform-profile/platf
 Date:		March 2025
 KernelVersion:	6.14
 Description:	Reading this file gives the current selected profile for this
-		device. Writing this file with one of the strings from
-		platform_profile_choices changes the profile to the new value.
+		device. Writing this file with one of the strings from choices
+		changes the profile to the new value.
 
 		This file can be monitored for changes by polling for POLLPRI,
 		POLLPRI will be signaled on any changes, independent of those
